Clean water is not a luxury — it is a basic human right. Yet too many communities in Nairobi County still walk kilometres for water that is not safe to drink. Bill Llia's infrastructure plan is built on a simple principle: prioritize the projects that change daily life, and hold every contractor and official accountable for delivering quality work on time and on budget.

**Water for every community:** Bill will accelerate borehole and water pan construction in the 20 most underserved wards within his first year, with a target of universal access to clean water within 1 kilometre of every household by the end of his first term. He will rehabilitate existing water supply systems that have fallen into disrepair, install community-managed water kiosks with affordable pricing, and partner with the national government and development partners to extend piped water to peri-urban areas.

**Roads that connect and deliver:** Good roads are the arteries of economic activity. Bill will establish a transparent county road maintenance fund — with published budgets and community oversight committees in every ward — to ensure that every shilling is spent where it matters most. Priority will go to roads that connect farming areas to markets, schools to communities, and health facilities to the families that depend on them.

**Street lighting for security and commerce:** Every market centre and major public space in the county will get solar-powered street lighting within two years. This is not just about visibility — it is about security for women and children, extended hours for small businesses, and safer streets for everyone.

**Public sanitation:** We will construct modern public sanitation facilities in every market centre and along major transport corridors, maintained through a combination of county funding and local management committees.

Bill Llia believes that infrastructure is not about ribbons and ceremonies. It is about whether a child can study after dark, a farmer can get produce to market, and a family can turn on a tap and trust what comes out.
